{"_v":3,"id":"i-became-we-off-broadway-2026","cat":"off-broadway","cs":83.96,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":5,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Helen Shaw","o":"The New York Times","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/28/theater/i-became-we-review-mona-pirnot.html","d":"2026-10-28","q":"The production is also consistently, ecstatically gorgeous.","dg":"Critics_Pick","tc":1},{"cn":null,"o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/page/ob/10_27_26.html","d":"2026-10-27","q":"I Became We is charming, funny, and surprisingly moving as it explores over the course of 70 minutes the notion of 'having it all.'"},{"cn":"Michael Sommers","o":"New York Stage Review","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://nystagereview.com/2026/10/27/i-became-we-modern-married-life/","d":"2026-10-27","q":"A sophisticated chamber musical of this quality is a rare event and should be grabbed with both hands."},{"cn":"Caroline Cao","o":"New York Theatre Guide","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.newyorktheatreguide.com/reviews/i-became-we-off-broadway-review","d":"2026-10-27","q":"It’s a moving 70 minutes on the uncertainties that can orbit a life."},{"cn":"Kenji Fujishima","o":"TheaterMania","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.theatermania.com/news/review-i-became-we-is-a-musical-monologue-about-thoughts-of-motherhood_1858228/","d":"2026-10-27","q":"In a show that offers a brilliant demonstration of the power of music to make deeply personal feelings broadly accessible, this moment carries the force of a universal epiphany."},{"cn":"Thom Geier","o":"Culture Sauce","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://culturesauce.com/i-became-we-off-broadway-review/","d":"2026-10-27","q":"I Became We is a singular achievement, a choral masterpiece that is thoughtful, smart, funny, and frankly unforgettable."},{"cn":null,"o":"Front Row Center","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://thefrontrowcenter.com/2026/10/i-became-we/","d":"2026-10-